#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:9
#: 2c0e632cc19846d783fefa5858b9ef73
msgid "The CLI is being phased out on all platforms. The features were massively cut down with AC3.1.5 and then it was removed for the APM2 completely anyway with AC3.2. All CLI functions are now available via regular MAVLink commands in the GCSs. This article has been moved to the dev wiki and may be considered deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:15
#: 60e16851cf6141f9be6ccf7c58699f9f
msgid "The Terminal tab is visible on the top icon row when \"Advanced View\" is checked in the Config tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:21
#: 35b03451de614425b5bf8ae36f366433
msgid "This section of Mission Planner, invoked by the Menu item Terminal at the top of Mission Planner, opens a window that allows communication with the auto pilot in a 'terminal' mode. This mode allows many actions specific to the auto pilot and specific to the control firmware in the autopilot. Copter, Plane and rovers will have different options. Refer to the vehicle specific area of the website for details about your specific platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:29
#: 12e2f651b2b945cd8a0bfbac071e79c4
msgid "Note:  When you open this menu item, the connection to your APM or PX4 will not be changed.  If connected, you will remain connected. This is to prevent loss of control in case you are in a mission or your vehicle is armed and in operation.  You must click the Connect APM or Connect PX4 button to use the features in this screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:38
#: 64362907c7c844c083a422ac32e12635
msgid "Screen Actions:  There are several buttons in this screen.  Here is the function of each:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:41
#: 64b620814be0431baf46fd6d1d2e654f
msgid "Connect APM:  Reboot the APM in CLI mode and enable this screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:42
#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:44
#: 2b66934775f845009594eb2226732174
#: 64183700336746dea2dd18b5f1de780f
msgid "Caution, previous connection will be lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:43
#: 1f3466aebae242b2860cc50423ad4f19
msgid "Connect PX4:  Reboot the PX4 in CLI mode and enable this screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:45
#: b2de2005e91142ab83be32796af9cb0e
msgid "Show Settings: This simply lists all the parameters in your auto pilot.  Better to use the Configuration Tuning section of Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:48
#: 2584a51e72064348a4b199512674eb41
msgid "Setup Radio: Goes to the setup section, radio and allows you to set up the radio.  Better to use the Configuration Tuning section of Mission Planner but sometimes this is useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:51
#: 040cfd837c374ebaae2dc9848cc1f5e0
msgid "Tests: Goes to the tests section of CLI and lists the options. You can type any of the options, press Enter to run the test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:53
#: 00c99944597340f880cef2485479f695
msgid "Log Download: Opens a new screen for downloading and performing other actions related to the Flash Data logs that are recorded in the auto pilot. These logs are recorded when the APM or PX4 is enabled and stopped when it is disabled.  See the links below for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-terminal.rst:58
#: a214dab5fcaa4cb09d583e7096a16347
msgid "Log Browse:  Lets you open a log file  (file with extension .log) that was previously saved and graph the various parameters that were recorded.  See the Data Flash Logs link below for more detail."
msgstr ""

